Modified for BenCode with MonoCode's recovery for a stalled display link
(MonoCode's `vendor/gpui-pre-macos`, commits 189d64a0, c341daf6, be06a810):

- src/display_link.rs: a shared link CoreVideo stopped behind the registry's
  back is started again (`CVDisplayLinkIsRunning`); a start is a failure only
  when the link really is stopped.
- src/window.rs: starting frames is idempotent and no longer stops them first;
  synchronous redraws (`windowDidBecomeKey:`, `displayLayer:`) keep the link
  running; `frame_waker` watches a window GPUI wants a frame for and restarts
  its link after 500ms without a tick (`watch_frames`); vsync frames yield to
  AppKit's redraws during a live resize; a dropped window counts as closed.

Everything else is the crates.io source unchanged. To move to a new
gpui-pre, copy its `gpui-pre-macos` here and carry those changes over.
